#! ia 1.0

@playbook host-lower
  meaning
    says "How a plugin is lowered into IA records: read its file tree and manifests, dry-run ia init --from, resolve every unresolved entry by fixing the plugin or stopping, apply, and keep the lowering map. Lowering never drops a construct."
    answers "What does an agent do to lower a plugin?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Read the plugin's file tree and its manifests; name the hosts it ships for."
      Inference means "List the files and frontmatter keys the lowering map must give a disposition."
      Decision means "Decide whether the plugin is in slice 1: hooks, MCP or LSP configuration, commands, agents with tools outside the effect table, non-UTF-8 files, CRLF, a byte-order mark and quote, backslash or control characters refuse."
      Learning means "Read earlier lowering maps in the kit before repeating their decisions."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what the lowering must keep: every file, every key, every byte of bodies, prompts and assets."
      Inference means "Run ia init <kit> --from <plugin> without --apply; read every unresolved entry; fix the plugin or stop, never drop a construct."
      Decision means "Order the fixes: one cause per unresolved entry, the smallest change to the plugin that clears it."
      Learning means "Say in the plan which dispositions you expect to be retired or derived, and why."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Watch the refusal: an unresolved entry means the plugin holds something the lowering cannot yet carry."
      Inference means "Stay with the dry run until it lists no unresolved entry; do not apply around a refusal."
      Decision means "Apply with --apply --yes; run ia validate on the new workspace."
      Learning means "Keep a failed apply on the record and rerun after the fix."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Verify the new workspace admits and holds every file the plan listed."
      Inference means "Have the independent reviewer check each retired or derived disposition and its reason."
      Decision means "Record the outcome and hand the workspace to host-project."
      Learning means "Keep assets/lowering-map.json and MIGRATION.md with the kit; report each retired or derived disposition."

@playbook host-project
  meaning
    says "How a lowered workspace is rendered back into a plugin: ia project --product plugin into an absent or empty directory, then --check --compare against the original, then the plugin's own tests."
    answers "What does an agent do to project and prove a plugin?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Read the lowered workspace and the original plugin it came from."
      Inference means "Name the output directory: it must be absent or empty."
      Decision means "Choose the host to project for and the product section it needs."
      Learning means "Read earlier round-trip results for this workspace."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate the fidelity bar: content-exact against the original and a fixed point when lowered again."
      Inference means "Plan the render: ia project <host> --product plugin --out <directory>, then --check --compare."
      Decision means "List every expected difference and the DIFF_RULES entry that names it."
      Learning means "State what would make the round trip fail before it runs."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Watch the render: a refusal names the file or rule that blocks it."
      Inference means "Render, then run --check --compare, then the plugin's own tests."
      Decision means "Fix the records, never the generated output, when a difference has no rule."
      Learning means "Keep failed renders on the record."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Run the fixed-point check and report it verbatim."
      Inference means "Have the independent reviewer check every regenerated difference against a rule."
      Decision means "Record the result and whether the plugin may retire."
      Learning means "Keep the comparison report with the kit; name each difference and its rule."

@playbook host-evaluate
  meaning
    says "How a skill's triggering is measured: draft the cases, have a reviewer freeze them, capture, write the config with its cap, run dev mode, then gate mode, and record the results as observations. The rules are the host-trigger-* conventions; the config shape is the kit asset assets/trigger-config.md."
    answers "What does an agent do to evaluate triggering?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Read the skill's description and its nearest neighbour skills."
      Inference means "List the model-invocable skills; only they need trigger evaluation."
      Decision means "Decide the requirement each skill's cases implement."
      Learning means "Read earlier evaluation observations for the skill."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate the budget: ten should-trigger and ten should-not prompts per skill, near misses included."
      Inference means "Draft the cases from the description and its neighbours, then have a reviewer freeze them before any scored run."
      Decision means "Capture the records with ia capture and write the config with its session cap."
      Learning means "State the arms, the model and the mode before any session starts."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Watch the cap: the runner refuses a plan over the cap before it writes anything, then writes its manifest before the first session."
      Inference means "Run dev mode first, one run per case on the cheaper model, then gate mode, three runs per case on the target model."
      Decision means "Never repeat failed cases selectively; any unlisted, incomplete or error session makes the run incomplete, written as complete false in results.json with exit 1, and it is reported as incomplete."
      Learning means "Run the original and the regenerated plugin side by side on the same cases; the arm ids are fixed as original and then regenerated, and the sessions interleave the arms."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Read results.json and the counts per arm with their Wilson intervals; exit 3 means the regenerated arm is worse beyond noise, that is the Newcombe 95% interval of the difference lies entirely below zero, and a run in which no session triggered the skill is refused as possibly blind."
      Inference means "Have a reviewer who did not draft the cases read the verdicts."
      Decision means "Record per-case verdicts as observations with their counts and uncertainty."
      Learning means "Keep the raw stream logs with the run and propose description fixes to the skill's owner."

@playbook host-qualify
  meaning
    says "How a plugin is qualified on its hosts: an isolated install, claude plugin validate --strict, claude plugin details, and the Codex smoke, each observation recorded as evidence."
    answers "What does an agent do to qualify a plugin on its hosts?"
  subject
    subject-word capability
  cognition
    orient
      primary Attention
      Attention means "Read the plugin's manifests and the hosts it names."
      Inference means "List the components it ships and the listing cost each host will see."
      Decision means "Decide which host features the plugin relies on."
      Learning means "Read earlier qualification observations for these hosts."
    plan
      primary Inference
      Attention means "Restate what qualification must show: it installs, it validates and its listing fits."
      Inference means "Plan the isolated install in a scratch configuration, never the user's logged-in one."
      Decision means "Order the checks: install, claude plugin validate --strict, claude plugin details, then the Codex smoke."
      Learning means "State which result would fail the plugin for each host."
    act
      primary Decision
      Attention means "Watch each command's exit code; a failed install ends the run for that host."
      Inference means "Install in isolation, run claude plugin validate --strict and claude plugin details, then the Codex smoke."
      Decision means "Report every command, exit code and output verbatim."
      Learning means "Keep failed qualifications on the record."
    learn
      primary Learning
      Attention means "Compare the component inventory and listing cost with the original plugin."
      Inference means "Have the independent reviewer read the observations against the plugin."
      Decision means "Record each observation as evidence for a host-feature row."
      Learning means "Name what remains unqualified and on which host."

